---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Footer from '~/components/Footer.astro';
import FAQ from '~/components/FAQ.astro';
import { SITE, AREAS } from '~/lib/site';

// Dedicated dominance page for "custom drapery st petersburg".
// Built May 11, 2026 to displace Gotcha Covered / Yelp / Joann's Interiors
// on a query where we currently sit at organic #7 (rank_absolute 11).
//
// Page design principles:
//   E-E-A-T  → first-person owner byline, 25-year experience signal, in-house
//              workroom address, named brand-partner authority, real-named
//              testimonials with neighborhood + project specifics.
//   LLM-bait → every H2/H3 answers a discrete question in 30-50 words at the
//              top of its section, then expands. Direct, citation-ready, dated.
//   2026 SEO → Article + Service + LocalBusiness + HowTo + FAQPage + Review
//              + AggregateRating + BreadcrumbList. Author + date + region.
//   Internal → every Pinellas neighborhood + adjacent service is deep-linked.

const PUBLISHED = '2026-05-11';
const UPDATED = '2026-08-21';

const AUTHOR = {
  name: 'Terry Popick',
  role: 'Owner & Lead Designer',
  bio: '25 years designing and installing custom drapery across Pinellas County. Custom Fabric Creations is locally based in St. Petersburg, FL, an authorized dealer for Hunter Douglas, Norman, Graber, Kravet, and Stout, with access to the broader Kravet-distributed designer fabric library.',
};

const FAQS = [
  {
    q: 'What is custom drapery, and how is it different from ready-made curtains?',
    a: 'Custom drapery is sewn to your exact window measurements in a workroom, using fabric you select from designer textile houses. Ready-made curtains come in standard widths and lengths (panels are typically 50 inches wide; lengths are 63, 84, 95, 108 inches). If your window does not match those standard sizes, which it rarely does, ready-made panels either gap on the sides, drag on the floor, or float above it. Custom drapery is the opposite: it is built to your window, your ceiling height, your hardware, and your fabric.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How much does custom drapery cost in St. Petersburg, FL?',
    a: 'A pair of lined floor-length custom drapery panels in a mid-range designer fabric typically runs $600 to $900 per window installed in Pinellas County. The full range is $400 to $1,500+ per window. Fabric is the biggest cost driver: a Kravet mid-line cotton-linen blend lands around $50 per yard; a Brunschwig & Fils embroidered silk can be $200+. Lining, interlining, motorized track systems, and specialty hardware add on. We provide itemized per-window quotes after the in-home consultation so you see exactly where the cost goes.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How long does custom drapery take to make and install in St. Petersburg?',
    a: 'Four to six weeks from approved fabric to installed panels. Fabric lead time from the mill is one to three weeks. Our St. Petersburg workroom turns most drapery projects in two to three weeks once fabric arrives. Installation by our in-house crew is typically a half-day. For closing-day or move-in timelines, rush options exist on most fabric lines.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What fabric brands does Custom Fabric Creations carry?',
    a: 'We are an authorized dealer for Hunter Douglas, Norman, Graber, Kravet, and Stout. Through our Kravet relationship we also access Lee Jofa, Brunschwig & Fils, GP & J Baker, and Crypton performance fabrics. We bring fabric samples to your home so you select fabrics against your actual walls and lighting before committing.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you motorize drapery, and is it worth it?',
    a: 'Yes. We install Hunter Douglas PowerView motorization and discuss other motorized systems at consultation. Motorization is worth it for tall windows (over 8 feet), heavy fabric panels, sliding glass doors, smart-home integrations, and aging-in-place clients who want hands-free operation. Ask for current pricing and motor options when you book your consultation.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What\'s the difference between drapery and curtains?',
    a: 'In Florida residential design, "drapery" usually refers to floor-length lined panels mounted on a decorative rod or concealed track, often pleated at the top. "Curtains" is the broader term and includes shorter, unlined, lighter-weight window treatments. Both are made from fabric. Drapery is more formal and tailored; curtains are typically more casual. We make both at Custom Fabric Creations.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Will custom drapery hold up to Florida sun and humidity in Pinellas County?',
    a: 'Yes, when the right fabric is specified. UV-rated linings, performance fabrics rated for UV (Crypton, Sunbrella indoor-outdoor lines), and proper lining/interlining all extend the life of drapery in Florida. For salt-air zones, Snell Isle, Tierra Verde, Sand Key, the barrier islands, we recommend moisture-resistant interlining and synthetic-blend or treated natural fibers appropriate for coastal conditions.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you offer financing for custom drapery projects?',
    a: 'Financing options may be available depending on the project, ask at your consultation and we will walk you through current options.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can you match existing drapery, or recreate panels from a fabric I already own?',
    a: 'Often, yes. If you own a discontinued fabric or have a single panel that needs a twin, bring it (or a swatch) to the consultation. We can match the trim, the lining, the header style, and the hem. Color matching is fabric-dependent, we will tell you honestly what is achievable.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Where is Custom Fabric Creations based, and which neighborhoods do you serve?',
    a: 'Custom Fabric Creations is locally based in St. Petersburg, FL. We design, fabricate, and install across all 14 Pinellas County neighborhoods, Downtown St. Pete, Historic Old Northeast, Snell Isle, Shore Acres, Tierra Verde, St. Pete Beach, Treasure Island, Clearwater, Sand Key, Belleair Shore, Seminole, Largo, and West St. Pete, plus the broader Tampa Bay area including Tampa, Brandon, Riverview, Apollo Beach, Tarpon Springs, and Palm Harbor.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why is a local workroom better than ordering custom drapery online?',
    a: 'Three reasons. (1) Measurement, measuring drapery requires accounting for stack-back, fullness ratio, return depth, mounting height, and floor break. Online calculators ignore most of these. (2) Fabric in person, fabric on a phone screen does not match fabric in your actual living room light. We bring 60-100 fabric memos to every consultation. (3) Accountability, if a panel hangs wrong, we are 20 minutes away. Online sellers leave the install to you.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you handle the hardware, or just the panels?',
    a: 'Both. Drapery hardware, rods, rings, finials, brackets, motorized tracks, ripplefold systems, ceiling-mount tracks, is half the look. We source decorative and concealed hardware from the same brands that the textile houses recommend. Installation is by our own crew, never a subcontractor.',
  },
];

const PROJECTS = [
  {
    neighborhood: 'Snell Isle',
    style: 'Mediterranean Revival waterfront',
    treatment: 'Kravet linen pinch-pleat sheers + blackout layer over the master bedroom\'s east-facing bay window.',
    image: '/images/gallery/master-suite-gallery.webp',
    alt: 'Custom Kravet linen drapery in a Snell Isle master suite, bay window with sheers layered over blackout panels, by Custom Fabric Creations, St. Petersburg, FL',
  },
  {
    neighborhood: 'Historic Old Northeast',
    style: '1920s Craftsman bungalow',
    treatment: 'Stout woven jacquard drapery on hand-finished oil-rubbed bronze hardware to match the original window trim.',
    image: '/images/gallery/contrast-drapery-gallery.webp',
    alt: 'Stout jacquard drapery in a Historic Old Northeast Craftsman bungalow, installed on oil-rubbed bronze hardware matching the original trim, by Custom Fabric Creations, St. Petersburg, FL',
  },
  {
    neighborhood: 'Downtown St. Pete',
    style: 'High-rise condo, floor-to-ceiling glass',
    treatment: 'Ceiling-mounted ripplefold sheers across a full window wall, even S-folds from a hidden track.',
    image: '/images/new/sheer-ripple-fold-drapery-bedroom.webp',
    alt: 'Ripple-fold sheer drapery on a ceiling-mounted track in a St. Petersburg bedroom by Custom Fabric Creations',
  },
  {
    neighborhood: 'Tierra Verde',
    style: 'Island home, salt-air exposure',
    treatment: 'Crypton performance-fabric drapery with marine-grade lining for the sliding-door wall to the lanai.',
    image: '/images/gallery/lanai-shading-gallery.webp',
    alt: 'Crypton performance-fabric drapery on a Tierra Verde lanai sliding door, marine-grade lining for salt-air exposure, by Custom Fabric Creations, FL',
  },
  {
    neighborhood: 'St. Pete Beach',
    style: 'Beachfront condo',
    treatment: 'UV-rated lined panels in a soft Brunschwig & Fils embroidered silk, with a coordinating box cornice.',
    image: '/images/gallery/custom-valances-gallery.webp',
    alt: 'Brunschwig & Fils embroidered silk drapery with a custom box cornice in a St. Pete Beach beachfront condo, UV-rated lining, by Custom Fabric Creations',
  },
  {
    neighborhood: 'Clearwater',
    style: 'Coastal modern',
    treatment: 'Floor-length linen pinch-pleat panels with stainless-steel rod and ceramic finials for an open-plan great room.',
    image: '/images/gallery/custom-drapery-gallery.webp',
    alt: 'Floor-length linen pinch-pleat drapery in a Clearwater coastal modern great room, stainless rod, ceramic finials, by Custom Fabric Creations, FL',
  },
];

const PRICING = [
  { kind: 'Sheer panels (linen / cotton blend)',           range: '$400 - $700',   fabric: 'mid-range Kravet, lined' },
  { kind: 'Blackout drapery panels (cotton / poly blend)', range: '$550 - $900',   fabric: 'Stout or Kravet, blackout lined' },
  { kind: 'Designer drapery (silk / embroidered)',         range: '$900 - $1,500+', fabric: 'Brunschwig & Fils, Lee Jofa, GP & J Baker' },
  { kind: 'Motorized drapery (per opening)',               range: '+$300 - $800',  fabric: 'add to any panel, Hunter Douglas PowerView + other systems' },
  { kind: 'Custom valance or cornice',                     range: '$350 - $850',   fabric: 'paired with drapery, same fabric or contrast' },
  { kind: 'Ripplefold track system (per opening)',         range: '$450 - $1,200', fabric: 'concealed track, modern minimalist style' },
];

// LLM-friendly structured FAQ for Schema.org/FAQPage
const faqsForSchema = FAQS;

// Custom HowTo schema for the 5-step process
const howToSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'HowTo',
  '@id': `${SITE.url}/custom-drapery-st-petersburg/#howto`,
  name: 'How Custom Drapery Is Designed, Made, and Installed in St. Petersburg, FL',
  description: 'A five-step process from in-home consultation to installed custom drapery, used by Custom Fabric Creations across Pinellas County since 2000.',
  totalTime: 'P6W',
  estimatedCost: { '@type': 'MonetaryAmount', currency: 'USD', value: '600' },
  supply: ['Designer fabric memos', 'Drapery hardware samples', 'Lining and interlining swatches'],
  tool:   ['Laser measure', 'Industrial workroom sewing machines', 'Steam press'],
  step: [
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 1, name: 'Free in-home consultation', text: 'Our designer brings a curated fabric library and hardware samples to your home. We walk every window, mark sizes, identify constraints, and recommend treatments and fabrics against your actual walls and light. Typically 90 minutes. No deposit required.' },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 2, name: 'Fabric selection and approval', text: 'We drop fabric memos for final review against your existing furniture and walls. You confirm fabric, lining, header style, hardware, and hem details. We finalize the written quote.' },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 3, name: 'Final measurement', text: 'Once hardware is approved and fabric is ordered, we return for a precise final measure to 1/16 inch. Stack-back, return depth, mounting height, and floor break are all captured.' },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 4, name: 'Workroom fabrication', text: 'Your panels are cut, sewn, and finished in our St. Petersburg workroom. Headers, linings, and hems are hand-finished by drapery specialists. Two to three weeks once fabric arrives.' },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 5, name: 'Installation', text: 'Our in-house crew installs hardware, hangs panels, steams out shipping creases, and confirms the fit on-site. You see the finished result before we call it done. Typically a half-day.' },
  ],
};

// Article schema with author + dates, E-E-A-T critical
const articleSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  '@id': `${SITE.url}/custom-drapery-st-petersburg/#article`,
  headline: 'Custom Drapery in St. Petersburg, FL: A 2026 Guide From a Local 25-Year Workroom',
  description: 'Everything St. Petersburg homeowners need to know about custom drapery in 2026, fabrics, pricing, process, neighborhoods, and how to choose a workroom. Written by Terry Popick, owner of Custom Fabric Creations.',
  author: {
    '@type': 'Person',
    name: AUTHOR.name,
    jobTitle: AUTHOR.role,
    worksFor: { '@id': `${SITE.url}/#organization` },
    description: AUTHOR.bio,
  },
  publisher: { '@id': `${SITE.url}/#organization` },
  datePublished: PUBLISHED,
  dateModified: UPDATED,
  mainEntityOfPage: `${SITE.url}/custom-drapery-st-petersburg/`,
  image: `${SITE.url}/images/services/custom-draperies-curtains/hero.webp`,
  about: { '@type': 'Service', name: 'Custom Drapery Installation' },
  spatialCoverage: {
    '@type': 'AdministrativeArea',
    name: 'Pinellas County, Florida',
    containedInPlace: { '@type': 'State', name: 'Florida' },
  },
};

// Service schema tied to the drapery work specifically
const serviceSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Service',
  '@id': `${SITE.url}/custom-drapery-st-petersburg/#service`,
  name: 'Custom Drapery in St. Petersburg, FL',
  serviceType: 'Custom Drapery Design, Fabrication & Installation',
  provider: { '@id': `${SITE.url}/#organization` },
  areaServed: [
    ...AREAS.map((a) => ({ '@type': 'City', name: a.title })),
    { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Pinellas County, FL' },
    { '@type': 'City', name: 'Tampa, FL' },
  ],
  offers: {
    '@type': 'AggregateOffer',
    priceCurrency: 'USD',
    lowPrice: '400',
    highPrice: '1500',
    priceSpecification: { '@type': 'UnitPriceSpecification', unitText: 'per window installed' },
  },
  hasOfferCatalog: {
    '@type': 'OfferCatalog',
    name: 'Custom drapery treatments',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'Offer', itemOffered: { '@type': 'Service', name: 'Sheer drapery panels' } },
      { '@type': 'Offer', itemOffered: { '@type': 'Service', name: 'Blackout drapery panels' } },
      { '@type': 'Offer', itemOffered: { '@type': 'Service', name: 'Designer drapery in silk and embroidered fabric' } },
      { '@type': 'Offer', itemOffered: { '@type': 'Service', name: 'Motorized drapery (Hunter Douglas PowerView and other systems)' } },
      { '@type': 'Offer', itemOffered: { '@type': 'Service', name: 'Ripplefold track drapery' } },
      { '@type': 'Offer', itemOffered: { '@type': 'Service', name: 'Cornices, valances, and top treatments' } },
    ],
  },
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Custom Drapery St. Petersburg, FL | Designer Workroom Since 2000, CFC"
  description="Custom drapery in St. Petersburg, FL from a 25-year local workroom. Designer fabrics from Kravet, Stout, Lee Jofa, and Brunschwig & Fils, sewn in-house and installed across Pinellas County and Tampa Bay. Free in-home consultation."
  pageType="article"
  articleDate={PUBLISHED}
  ogImage="/images/services/custom-draperies-curtains/hero.webp"
  faqs={faqsForSchema}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Custom Drapery St. Petersburg', url: '/custom-drapery-st-petersburg/' },
  ]}
>
  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-ink-900">
    <div class="absolute inset-0">
      <img
        src="/images/services/custom-draperies-curtains/hero.webp"
        alt="Formal gold drapery with a swag-and-jabot valance over sheers in a St. Petersburg, FL dining room by Custom Fabric Creations"
        title="Custom drapery in St. Petersburg, FL, Custom Fabric Creations"
        class="w-full h-full object-cover"
        fetchpriority="high"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-b from-ink-900/70 via-ink-900/55 to-ink-900/85"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="relative container-site text-center py-28 md:py-40 lg:py-48">
      <nav class="mb-6 flex items-center justify-center gap-2.5 text-sm md:text-base tracking-wide text-white/85 font-medium" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-brand-300 transition">Home</a>
        <span class="text-brand-400">/</span>
        <span class="text-brand-300">Custom Drapery St. Petersburg</span>
      </nav>

      <p class="flex justify-center items-center gap-3 mb-5 text-brand-300">
        <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase" style="letter-spacing: 0.3em;">St. Petersburg's Designer Drapery Workroom Since 2000</span>
      </p>

      <h1 class="font-display mx-auto max-w-5xl leading-[1.05] text-5xl sm:text-6xl md:text-7xl lg:text-[5rem] text-white">
        Custom Drapery in St. Petersburg, FL
      </h1>

      <p class="mt-6 text-lg md:text-xl max-w-3xl mx-auto leading-relaxed text-white/90">
        Designer drapery panels, sheers, blackout treatments, and motorized track systems, measured in your home, sewn in our St. Pete workroom, and installed by the same team that designed them. 25 years. Hundreds of Pinellas homes. Eighteen fabric brands on hand.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-4 justify-center">
        <a href="/contact/" class="btn-primary btn-lg">Schedule In-Home Consultation</a>
        <a href={SITE.phoneHref} class="btn-outline btn-lg">Call {SITE.phone}</a>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-6 max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center">
        <div>
          <p class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl text-brand-400">25+</p>
          <p class="text-[0.7rem] tracking-[0.22em] uppercase text-white/75 font-semibold mt-1">Years in St. Pete</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl text-brand-400">700+</p>
          <p class="text-[0.7rem] tracking-[0.22em] uppercase text-white/75 font-semibold mt-1">5-Star Reviews</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl text-brand-400">14</p>
          <p class="text-[0.7rem] tracking-[0.22em] uppercase text-white/75 font-semibold mt-1">Pinellas Areas</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl text-brand-400">18</p>
          <p class="text-[0.7rem] tracking-[0.22em] uppercase text-white/75 font-semibold mt-1">Fabric Brands</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- AUTHOR / BYLINE BAR, E-E-A-T -->
  <section class="bg-cream-50 border-b border-line">
    <div class="container-narrow py-6 md:py-7 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
        <div class="w-14 h-14 rounded-full bg-brand-500 text-white flex items-center justify-center font-display text-lg font-bold shrink-0">TP</div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-500">Reviewed by</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-ink-800">{AUTHOR.name} <span class="text-ink-500 font-normal">- {AUTHOR.role}, Custom Fabric Creations</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="text-xs text-ink-500 tracking-wide">
        <p><span class="uppercase font-semibold text-ink-700">Published:</span> May 11, 2026</p>
        <p><span class="uppercase font-semibold text-ink-700">Last updated:</span> May 11, 2026</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- TL;DR, Direct AI Overview / LLM citation bait -->
  <section class="bg-white py-12 md:py-16">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <div class="bg-cream-50 border-l-4 border-brand-500 p-6 md:p-8 rounded-sm">
        <p class="eyebrow mb-3" style="letter-spacing: 0.3em;">Quick Answer</p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl text-ink-800 mb-4 leading-tight">What custom drapery in St. Petersburg, FL means in 2026</h2>
        <p class="text-ink-600 leading-relaxed text-lg">
          Custom drapery in St. Petersburg is drapery panels measured to your exact windows, sewn from designer-house fabrics (Kravet, Stout, Lee Jofa, Brunschwig &amp; Fils), and installed by a local workroom. In Pinellas County, the typical custom drapery project runs <strong>$400-$1,500 per window installed</strong>, takes <strong>4-6 weeks</strong> from approved fabric to install, and lasts <strong>10-15 years</strong> in Florida-rated fabric. Custom Fabric Creations has been making and installing custom drapery in St. Petersburg since 2000.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 1: THREE TIERS, visual comparison cards -->
  <section id="what-is-custom-drapery" class="bg-white py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="container-site">
      <div class="text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-14">
        <p class="eyebrow mb-3" style="letter-spacing: 0.3em;">The Three Tiers</p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-5xl text-ink-800 mb-5 leading-tight">Three kinds of drapery you can buy.<br/><span class="text-brand-700">Only one is actually custom.</span></h2>
        <p class="text-ink-600 text-lg leading-relaxed">If your window does not match a manufactured standard, and most St. Pete windows don't, only one of these three options will fit. Here is how they compare.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3 max-w-6xl mx-auto">
        <!-- TIER 1: Ready-made -->
        <div class="bg-cream-50 border border-line rounded-sm overflow-hidden flex flex-col">
          <div class="bg-ink-700 text-white px-6 py-4">
            <p class="text-[0.65rem] tracking-[0.22em] uppercase text-white/70 font-semibold mb-1">Tier 1</p>
            <h3 class="font-display text-2xl text-white">Ready-made</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="p-6 flex-1 flex flex-col">
            <div class="mb-5">
              <p class="text-[0.65rem] tracking-[0.18em] uppercase text-ink-500 font-semibold mb-1">Per panel</p>
              <p class="font-display text-3xl text-ink-800">$30 - $300</p>
            </div>
            <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm text-ink-700 leading-relaxed mb-6 flex-1">
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-ink-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5">●</span><span>Fixed widths (usually 50") and 4 fixed lengths (63, 84, 95, 108")</span></li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-ink-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5">●</span><span>Pre-sewn, off-the-shelf, fits what fits, gaps the rest</span></li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-ink-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5">●</span><span>Unrated linings, fade in Florida sun within 18-36 months</span></li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-ink-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5">●</span><span>You install</span></li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-500 pt-4 border-t border-line">Pottery Barn, West Elm, Target, Amazon</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- TIER 2: Semi-custom -->
        <div class="bg-cream-50 border border-line rounded-sm overflow-hidden flex flex-col">
          <div class="bg-ink-800 text-white px-6 py-4">
            <p class="text-[0.65rem] tracking-[0.22em] uppercase text-white/70 font-semibold mb-1">Tier 2</p>
            <h3 class="font-display text-2xl text-white">Semi-custom</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="p-6 flex-1 flex flex-col">
            <div class="mb-5">
              <p class="text-[0.65rem] tracking-[0.18em] uppercase text-ink-500 font-semibold mb-1">Per panel</p>
              <p class="font-display text-3xl text-ink-800">$200 - $700</p>
            </div>
            <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm text-ink-700 leading-relaxed mb-6 flex-1">
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-ink-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5">●</span><span>Choose from preset widths + lengths, closer to your window, not exact</span></li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-ink-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5">●</span><span>Limited supplier-curated fabric list</span></li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-ink-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5">●</span><span>Install usually not included</span></li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-ink-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5">●</span><span>Returns are difficult once cut</span></li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-500 pt-4 border-t border-line">Pottery Barn Custom, Restoration Hardware, Calico Corners</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- TIER 3: Fully custom (us) -->
        <div class="bg-white border-2 border-brand-500 rounded-sm overflow-hidden flex flex-col shadow-soft relative">
          <div class="absolute top-4 right-4 bg-brand-500 text-white px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-[0.65rem] uppercase tracking-[0.15em] font-bold">You are here</div>
          <div class="bg-brand-500 text-white px-6 py-4">
            <p class="text-[0.65rem] tracking-[0.22em] uppercase text-white/80 font-semibold mb-1">Tier 3, what CFC makes</p>
            <h3 class="font-display text-2xl text-white">Fully custom</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="p-6 flex-1 flex flex-col">
